      "content": "Thanks, this is a good start. It's clear and covers the basics.\n\nI just ran it through the pre-submission audit tool, and the score is actually pretty low—like, it's barely scraping the minimum threshold for the technical density check. I think it's because the sentences are a bit too \"standard\" in their phrasing. \n\nThe board is going to be looking for extreme precision here. Can you refine this? We need to push that jargon score way up so it passes the audit comfortably. Try to incorporate more specific terminology related to the molecular mechanisms, the LNP lipid compositions, and the specific statistical/analytical parameters for the flow cytometry. \n\nAgain, just make sure it still actually describes the experiment correctly. Don't just throw in words for the sake of it, but definitely lean into the high-level technicality.",
