      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The therapeutic modality utilizes a precision CRISPR/Cas9 system directed against the $\\text{HBB}$ locus employing a multiplexed dual-guide RNA cassette complexed with a high-fidelity $\\text{Cas}9$ variant, such as $\\text{Cas}9\\text{HF}1$. Delivery is achieved via $\\text{LNPs}$ formulated with ionizable cationic lipids (e.g., $\\text{DOTAP}$ derivatives) engineered for endosomal escape within $\\text{CD}34^+ / \\text{CD}38^-$ hematopoietic stem and progenitor cells. Following nucleofection, the cellular population is subjected to optimized culture conditions to maximize HDR kinetics, facilitating precise point mutation correction. Editing efficiency and indel formation will be assayed via intracellular flow cytometry, employing $\\text{qPCR}$-based allele frequency determination and performing $\\text{T-cell}$ sorting coupled with spectral analysis to monitor on-target knock-in rates and $\\text{MHC}$-restricted off-target burden.",
      "source": "target",
