      "content": "That's a huge improvement on the technicality level. The audit score jumped significantly with those additions like the ionizable cationic lipids and the specific cell markers.\n\nI actually just ran it again, and while it's much better, we're still sitting in a \"yellow\" zone for the density metric. The reviewers at this level are used to seeing incredibly dense, information-heavy prose where every single phrase is packed with specific biochemical or genomic descriptors. \n\nCan we do one more pass to really maximize that density? I'm talking about expanding on the specific structural components of the LNP-mRNA-sgRNA complex, the precise enzymatic pathways involved in the DNA repair phase, and maybe even the specific fluorophores or compensation matrices we'd use in the flow cytometry. \n\nI really don't want this to become an unreadable word salad—I need the actual science to remain sound—but please, do not hold back on the technical terminology. We need that score to be in the \"green\" zone to ensure it isn't flagged for lack of rigor.",
